"VERIFIED"},"occurrences":[]},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1131068-i20230204","date":"2023-02-04","inspection_type":"Investigation of a report (self-reported)","result":"Deficiencies cited","passed":false,"violation_count":4,"open_count":0,"evidence_class":"VERIFIED","provenance":{"source_id":"tx_hhsc_activities","source_record_id":"905923765","url":"https://data.texas.gov/resource/m5q4-3y3d.json?activity_id=905923765","retrieved_at":"2026-11-05T21:27:29.718Z","effective_date":"2023-02-04","evidence_class":"VERIFIED"},"occurrences":[{"id":"tx-hhsc-1131068-i20230204-v1","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-1013-a-2","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1131068-i20230204","date":"2023-02-04","original_code":"746.1013(a)(2)","severity":"medium","severity_label":"Medium risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2023-03-08","finding":"Director's Absence -  Caregiver in Charge Knows Responsibilities: It was found during the investigation that at the time of the gas leak the person left in charge of the facility did not follow/know all the steps outlined in their Emergency Preparedness Plan. It was found that the planned evacuation routes for each class were not followed and instead of evacuating to the planned evacuation site stated in their Emergency Preparedness Plan they evacuated to the playground.  It was also found that the gates on the playground were locked, and the employees present at the time of the evacuation did not know the location of the keys to unlock the gates therefore they were unable to exit through the playground gates.","topic":"staffing","source_record_id":"1026649176","violation_type_title":"Director's Absence -  Caregiver in Charge Knows Responsibilities (26 TAC §746.1013(a)(2))","topic_label":"Staff qualifications & clearances"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1131068-i20230204-v2","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-601-c","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1131068-i20230204","date":"2023-02-04","original_code":"746.601(c)","severity":"medium","severity_label":"Medium risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2023-02-08","finding":"Provide Access to Children's Records - Licensing: The facility did not have 3 of 14 records avialble for review during in the inspection.","topic":"safety","source_record_id":"1026645821","violation_type_title":"Provide Access to Children's Records - Licensing (26 TAC §746.601(c))","topic_label":"Safety hazards"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1131068-i20230204-v3","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-1201-1","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1131068-i20230204","date":"2023-02-04","original_code":"746.1201(1)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2023-03-08","finding":"Responsibilities of Employees and Caregivers -Demonstrate Competency, Good Judgment, Self-control: Based on evidence obtained during the investigation it was found that the person in charge of the operation at the time of the incident did not use good judgement by reentering the building after they were told to evacuate the building by a gas company professional and allowing parents and children to reenter the building without receiving clearance from the gas company professionals to reenter.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026650814","violation_type_title":"Responsibilities of Employees and Caregivers -Demonstrate Competency, Good Judgment, Self-control (26 TAC §746.1201(1))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1131068-i20230204-v4","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-5202-3","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1131068-i20230204","date":"2023-02-04","original_code":"746.5202(3)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2023-03-08","finding":"Emergency Preparedness Plan - Essential Documentation: It was found during the investigation that the operation staff did not evacuate with the authorization for emergency care documents for each child in care.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026649286","vi